Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usages
• ball_by_ball.match_id: joins every delivery to its match.  
• ball_by_ball.over_id , ball_by_ball.ball_id: identify each legal ball in an over (6 legal balls = 1 over).  
• ball_by_ball.bowler: the bowler who delivered the ball ― fundamental for every bowling‑related metric.  
• batsman_scored.match_id / over_id / ball_id / runs_scored: number of runs “off the bat”; add them for the bowler’s runs‑conceded figure (economy, best figures).  
• extra_runs.match_id / over_id / ball_id / extra_runs / extra_type: to be excluded from the “runs conceded” computation requested.  
• wicket_taken.match_id / over_id / ball_id / player_out / kind_out / innings_no: shows every dismissal; filter out kinds such as 'run out' (and other non‑bowler dismissals) when counting wickets.  
• player.player_id / player_name: translates an ID to a readable bowler name.  
• match.match_id / match_date / season_id: helps when we need to label the “best” performance with the proper match.  

Typical conditions  
• wicket_taken.kind_out NOT IN ('run out', 'retired hurt', 'obstructing the field')  -- keep only bowler‑credited dismissals.  
• extra_runs.extra_type IN ('wides','noballs')  -- identify extras that must be ignored for economy.  
• JOIN keys: (match_id, over_id, ball_id) across ball_by_ball ↔ batsman_scored ↔ wicket_taken ↔ extra_runs.  

Exploratory SQL queries  
Below are ten progressively richer queries (each capped at 20 rows) that you could run to inspect the data before writing the final aggregation.

```sql
--1. List a few distinct bowlers who appear in ball_by_ball
SELECT DISTINCT bowler
FROM ball_by_ball
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--2. See what dismissal kinds exist, so we know what to exclude
SELECT DISTINCT kind_out
FROM wicket_taken
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--3. Inspect how batsman runs line up with individual deliveries
SELECT b.match_id, b.over_id, b.ball_id, b.bowler,
       bs.runs_scored
FROM ball_by_ball AS b
LEFT JOIN batsman_scored AS bs
  ON b.match_id = bs.match_id
 AND b.over_id  = bs.over_id
 AND b.ball_id  = bs.ball_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--4. Example of deliveries that also have an extra recorded
SELECT b.match_id, b.over_id, b.ball_id, b.bowler,
       e.extra_type, e.extra_runs
FROM ball_by_ball AS b
JOIN extra_runs AS e
  ON b.match_id = e.match_id
 AND b.over_id  = e.over_id
 AND b.ball_id  = e.ball_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--5. Raw count of wickets per bowler (all kinds)
SELECT b.bowler, COUNT(*) AS total_wickets
FROM ball_by_ball AS b
JOIN wicket_taken AS w
  ON b.match_id = w.match_id
 AND b.over_id  = w.over_id
 AND b.ball_id  = w.ball_id
GROUP BY b.bowler
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--6. Filtered count of bowler‑credited wickets (exclude run‑outs)
SELECT b.bowler, COUNT(*) AS bowler_wkts
FROM ball_by_ball AS b
JOIN wicket_taken AS w
  ON b.match_id = w.match_id
 AND b.over_id  = w.over_id
 AND b.ball_id  = w.ball_id
WHERE w.kind_out NOT IN ('run out')
GROUP BY b.bowler
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--7. Total balls delivered by each bowler (used for strike rate)
SELECT bowler, COUNT(*) AS balls_bowled
FROM ball_by_ball
GROUP BY bowler
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--8. Runs conceded off the bat by each bowler
SELECT b.bowler,
       SUM(IFNULL(bs.runs_scored,0)) AS runs_conceded
FROM ball_by_ball AS b
LEFT JOIN batsman_scored AS bs
  ON b.match_id = bs.match_id
 AND b.over_id  = bs.over_id
 AND b.ball_id  = bs.ball_id
GROUP BY b.bowler
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--9. Per‑match wicket haul of every bowler (for “best figures”)
SELECT b.match_id, b.bowler,
       COUNT(*) AS wkts_in_match
FROM ball_by_ball AS b
JOIN wicket_taken AS w
  ON b.match_id = w.match_id
 AND b.over_id  = w.over_id
 AND b.ball_id  = w.ball_id
WHERE w.kind_out NOT IN ('run out')
GROUP BY b.match_id, b.bowler
ORDER BY wkts_in_match DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10. Put everything together: wickets, balls, runs conceded, economy, strike rate, best figures
SELECT
    p.player_name                                       AS bowler_name,
    agg.total_wkts,
    ROUND(1.0*agg.runs_conceded / (agg.balls_bowled/6.0), 2) AS economy_rate,
    ROUND(1.0*agg.balls_bowled / agg.total_wkts, 2)          AS strike_rate,
    printf('%d-%d', best.max_wkts, best.runs_in_that_match)  AS best_figures
FROM
    ( /* overall aggregates per bowler */
      SELECT
          b.bowler,
          COUNT(w.player_out)                   AS total_wkts,
          COUNT(*)                              AS balls_bowled,
          SUM(IFNULL(bs.runs_scored,0))         AS runs_conceded
      FROM ball_by_ball AS b
      LEFT JOIN batsman_scored AS bs
        ON b.match_id = bs.match_id
       AND b.over_id  = bs.over_id
       AND b.ball_id  = bs.ball_id
      LEFT JOIN wicket_taken AS w
        ON b.match_id = w.match_id
       AND b.over_id  = w.over_id
       AND b.ball_id  = w.ball_id
       AND w.kind_out NOT IN ('run out')
      GROUP BY b.bowler
    ) AS agg
JOIN player            AS p    ON p.player_id = agg.bowler
JOIN
    ( /* best performance (match figures) */
      SELECT x.bowler,
             MAX(x.wkts)            AS max_wkts,
             MIN(x.runs_when_max)   AS runs_in_that_match
      FROM (
            SELECT b.match_id,
                   b.bowler,
                   COUNT(w.player_out)         AS wkts,
                   SUM(IFNULL(bs.runs_scored,0)) AS runs_when_max
            FROM ball_by_ball AS b
            LEFT JOIN batsman_scored AS bs
              ON b.match_id = bs.match_id
             AND b.over_id  = bs.over_id
             AND b.ball_id  = bs.ball_id
            LEFT JOIN wicket_taken AS w
              ON b.match_id = w.match_id
             AND b.over_id  = w.over_id
             AND b.ball_id  = w.ball_id
             AND w.kind_out NOT IN ('run out')
            GROUP BY b.match_id, b.bowler
           ) AS x
      GROUP BY x.bowler
    ) AS best
    ON best.bowler = agg.bowler
LIMIT 20;
```
